NO COPYLEFT DEPENDENCY
======================

Every module above is MIT, BSD-3-Clause, or Apache-2.0. kdbx has **no GPL,
LGPL, AGPL, or other copyleft dependency**, direct or transitive, at build time
or at run time. This was verified by scanning the license file of every module
in `go list -m all` for GNU General/Lesser/Affero Public License text; there
were no matches.

This is a deliberate difference from the Python implementation in
github.com/yarrasys/extensions, which depends on `pykeepass` (GPL-3.0) for its
KDBX engine. Because Python resolves that dependency at run time, the Python
skill could not bundle it and had to fetch it on each invocation, and its
license had to be recorded separately. kdbx ships as a single statically linked
binary with a permissive-only dependency tree, so it can be redistributed —
Homebrew, container images, vendored into other tools — without a copyleft
obligation attaching to it.


